  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Most ecommerce teams still treat their product feed as a Merchant Center compliance task.

Get the products approved.
Fix the errors.
Keep the feed live.
Move on.

But Google’s Shopping Graph has changed the role of product data.
It now helps power Shopping Ads, free listings, AI Overviews, AI Mode, Gemini, and other AI-led shopping experiences. That means product data is no longer just a feed. It is a visibility layer.

If your product titles are generic, your attributes are missing, your categories are shallow, or your price and availability data is stale, Google has less context to work with.

That matters. Because AI shopping experiences rely on structured product data to understand:
• What the product is
 • Who it is for
 • Which searches it matches
 • Whether the data can be trusted
 • Whether the product should be shown

Merchant Center approval is now the floor. The real opportunity is helping Google understand your products better.

Read the full guide here: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gPgrnm48?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gPgrnm48</a>

